## Why This Is Asked
Assess real-world offline sync with Core Data + CloudKit, conflict resolution, and test coverage.

## Key Concepts
- Core Data models and CloudKit integration
- Offline write queue and conflict resolution
- Versioning and user-facing conflict flow
- Test strategies for Multi-Device sync

## Code Example
```javascript
// Swift-like pseudo-model for Note
class Note: NSManagedObject {
  @NSManaged var id: UUID
  @NSManaged var title: String?
  @NSManaged var body: String?
  @NSManaged var updatedAt: Date
  @NSManaged var tags: [String]?
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test conflict resolution deterministically?
- What telemetry would you add to monitor sync health across devices?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests Core Data modeling, camera barcode scanning, SwiftUI lists, offline-first sync, and straightforward conflict resolution.

## Key Concepts

- Core Data model for Asset with versioning
- Barcode scanning with AVCaptureSession
- SwiftUI: List with Section by location
- Offline-first sync to REST API
- Conflict resolution: last-write-wins or server-based timestamp

## Code Example

```swift
class Asset: NSManagedObject {
  @NSManaged var tag: String
  @NSManaged var name: String
  @NSManaged var location: String
  @NSManaged var scannedAt: Date
  @NSManaged var version: Int32
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test barcode scanning accuracy across lighting conditions?
- How would you handle concurrent scans from multiple devices for the same asset?
